The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by calling gpioTerminate() and exiting the program gracefully.

Please note that the HC-SR04 operates at 5V and the Raspberry Pi GPIO is only 3.3V tolerant. Therefore, a 1kΩ resistor should be used on the echo line to protect the Raspberry Pi from damage.

Also, the program assumes that the echo signal is high for the duration of the sound wave and low for the duration of the return signal. If the echo signal is low for the duration of the sound wave and high for the duration of the return signal, you will need to reverse the logic in the while loop.

