This program reads from four BH1750FVI sensors attached to I2C-1, waits 180ms after each start-conversion command, and repeats this acquisition loop once per second. It then broadcasts a UDP multicast packet containing a semicolon-separated list of sensor_id,lux pairs. The program can be terminated by sending a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

Please note that you need to install the wiringPi library and the I2C tools on your Raspberry Pi before you can compile and run this program.

Also, the BH1750FVI sensor needs to be configured to work in a mode that allows for a 180ms measurement time. The default configuration is for a 120ms measurement time.

